# Base URL for the API. Leave unset — this should stay unset in every normal deployment of this
# app, including production.
#
# Locally, Vite's dev proxy (vite.config.js) forwards "/api" to the local server, so client and
# server share an origin. On Vercel, client/vercel.json's rewrite forwards "/api/*" to the deployed
# Render backend at the edge, so the browser still only ever talks to one origin (the Vercel
# domain) — this is deliberate, not a shortcut: the login cookie is set by whatever host the
# browser thinks it's talking to, and a genuinely cross-site request (client calling the Render
# URL directly) gets treated as a third-party cookie by the browser and silently blocked in
# Incognito/private browsing (and increasingly in normal browsing too). Routing through the same
# origin avoids that entirely.
#
# Only set this if you're deploying somewhere without rewrite/proxy support and are accepting the
# direct-cross-origin tradeoff above — point it at the deployed server's absolute URL, including
# the "/api" prefix, e.g.: VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://your-app.onrender.com/api"
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
